{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And Moses and Aaron came into the Tent of Meeting, and they came out and blessed the people.</b> The two of them entered there so that Moses might teach him the procedure of the incense offering, for during all seven days of ordination Aaron was not permitted to enter within the entrance of the Tent of Meeting, as it is written: ״At the entrance of the Tent of Meeting you shall sit״ etc., and now on the eighth day he was permitted to enter there, and Moses entered with him to teach him the procedure of the incense offering. For Moses had been offering the sacrifices at first and burning the incense, as you find in all the rites: ״And Moses took״ and ״And Moses sprinkled״ and ״And Moses placed״ and ״And he burned upon it incense of spices״ — for until this eighth day, when Aaron was ordained into the priesthood and began the divine service, Moses had been engaged in all the rites in their entirety, and he was the first priest; and Scripture does indeed call him a priest, as it is said (Psalms 99:6): ״משה ואהרן בכהניו״. And it says: ״And they came out and blessed the people״ — that is, immediately adjacent to the burning of the incense, for at that time prayer is more readily accepted. And so was the practice of the High Priest on Yom HaKippurim: he would enter the innermost sanctuary to burn the incense and leave the firepan inside and go out and pray concerning the needs of the people — for sufficiency of their sustenance and food, for the descent of rain, and for the rest of their needs. And from this David, peace be upon him, said (Psalms 141): ״תכון תפלתי קטרת לפניך״ — he mentioned the incense more than the other offerings because it is the choicest and most favorably accepted offering, and prayer at that time is more readily accepted."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:24:21.429521640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}